mplaints into statutory Class C hazard buckets (lead paint, severe leaks/plumbing/mold, vermin/rodents, and safety hazards), aggregate distinct apartments and stories cited for Class C violations over 1y and 3y lookbacks, calculate 3-year consecutive Class C recidivism indicators, and compute rolling 1y, 3y, and cumulative DOB safety counts and tax lien sale flags. Interface constraints: Preserve the function signatures of extract_features(bbl_list, cutoff_date) and compute_labels(bbl_list, cutoff_date, violations_df), maintaining uniform feat_ prefixed feature columns and zero-imputation across 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, and 2023 cohorts.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Expand the training data by extracting features and labels for the pre-pandemic 2019-01-01 cohort alongside 2020 and 2021 cohorts, and apply exponential temporal decay sample weighting to training instances (0.5 for 2019, 0.7 for 2020, 1.0 for 2021) across LightGBM, XGBoost, and CatBoost models. WHY: The 2020 cohort was severely distorted by pandemic-era inspection halts and court suspensions; incorporating the 2019 cohort provides a clean, pre-COVID enforcement baseline that stabilizes feature splits, while temporal sample weighting focuses gradient updates on the modern enforcement regime matching the 2022 validation and 2023 test windows. HOW: Extract features and compute labels for train_bbls at t_train_2019 = pd.Timestamp('2019-01-01'), concatenate 2019, 2020, and 2021 DataFrames into df_train_feat, construct a sample_weight array based on cohort year, and pass sample_weight to lgb_clf.fit(), xgb_clf.fit(), and cb_clf.fit() while evaluating against the untouched 2022 validation hold-out. Interface constraints: Maintain X_train_raw, y_train, X_val_raw, y_val, and X_test_raw variable definitions, preserve the 3-model convex rank-percentile blend search, and output final test predictions to submission/submission.csv with 171,587 rows and columns bbl and score."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response"